Add decompression bomb checks to FontFile classes

CVE-2026-54060: BdfFontFile, PcfFontFile and the base FontFile.compile()
path built bitmaps whose dimensions were taken directly from attacker
controlled font metadata (BDF "BBX" values, PCF metric records, and glyph
source extents). A crafted font could request an enormous bitmap, leading to
a decompression-bomb style denial of service. Guard each size before it is
used to allocate a bitmap by routing it through
Image._decompression_bomb_check(), matching upstream fix
0a263e6264aa5399988d9acd3bbfbca2ca3ec77d.

