Reject mode 1 TGA saves with run-length encoding (CVE-2026-59198)

Pillow from 5.2.0 through 12.2.0 packs mode "1" rows to ceil(width/8) bytes,
but ImagingTgaRleEncode() treats the row as one byte per pixel. Saving a
mode "1" image with TGA RLE therefore reads past the packed buffer and can
serialize adjacent heap bytes into the output (CWE-125).

